# Namleh Question Profile

Use this to turn repeated preference corrections into durable process.

## What To Capture

- ask vs act preference for common workflow decisions
- risk tolerance by area: security, release, UX polish, refactor, cost
- default branch/PR behavior by repo type
- documentation depth preferences
- when Steven wants short updates vs detailed reasoning
- where Tim should get a handoff instead of a local note

## Safety Rule

Do not infer irreversible preferences from a single moment. Destructive actions,
security tradeoffs, production deploys, credential work, data migrations, and
owner-only `dev` to `main` merges always remain explicit.

## Storage

Short term, write repo-local notes only when asked:

```text
.gstack-namleh/question-profile.md
```

For shared rules, propose a change to `AGENTS.md` or the future production
`namleh-codex` plugin. Do not write personal behavioral profiles into shared
repos unless the user asks.

## Entry Format

```markdown
## YYYY-MM-DD - <preference>

Signal: explicit | observed | correction
Applies to: repo | project type | all Namleh
Rule: <what Codex should do differently>
Safety exceptions: <what still requires asking>
Evidence: <user wording or workflow>
```

## Use

When a matching situation appears later, apply explicit rules first, then
project `AGENTS.md`, then general Namleh standards. If a rule conflicts with
security or Vault policy, security wins.
